                        "entry_id": "7aa34c1a-5e90-3e6f-a29b-4343c3cb3cf8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A form of pension or annuity given by a religious institution as provision for maintenance."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "historical",
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4986e445-6103-44aa-beae-8f4758c2e558",
                                "sense_id": "5f17a0e9-6df2-3a1f-aafe-772f2fc60746",
                                "text": "The corrody became first and foremost a grant of money or victuals, or other means of livelihood, made by a monastery or other religious or charitable corporation to dependents on its bounty."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "031915a8-de34-43c6-9c9c-cc2fdfa9a58d",
                                "sense_id": "5f17a0e9-6df2-3a1f-aafe-772f2fc60746",
                                "text": "Corrodies were of three kinds: retirement arrangements for former abbots and priors; private deals struck by outsiders to provide board and lodging, in return for gifts of cash or property; and […] grants to crown servants."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
